Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• `objects.object_id`: join‐key between `objects` and `images`  
• `objects.department`: keep only rows where department = 'Photographs'  
• `objects.object_name`: look for the term “Photograph” (e.g. WHERE LOWER(object_name) LIKE '%photograph%')  
• `objects.artist_display_name`: exclude “Unknown” (e.g. WHERE LOWER(artist_display_name) NOT LIKE 'unknown%')  
• `objects.object_end_date`: require 1839 or earlier (e.g. WHERE object_end_date <= 1839)  
• `objects.title`: return in the final answer  
• `objects.medium`: return in the final answer  
• `images.object_id`: join‐key to `objects`  
• `images.original_image_url`: return in the final answer  

Typical filter conditions  
• `department = 'Photographs'`  
• `LOWER(object_name) LIKE '%photograph%'`  
• `object_end_date <= 1839`  
• `LOWER(artist_display_name) NOT LIKE 'unknown%'`  

Below are ten exploratory / incremental queries (each returns ≤ 20 rows) that gradually build toward the final answer.  

```sql
