Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• `objects.object_id`: join‐key between `objects` and `images`  
• `objects.department`: keep only rows where department = 'Photographs'  
• `objects.object_name`: look for the term “Photograph” (e.g. WHERE LOWER(object_name) LIKE '%photograph%')  
• `objects.artist_display_name`: exclude “Unknown” (e.g. WHERE LOWER(artist_display_name) NOT LIKE 'unknown%')  
• `objects.object_end_date`: require 1839 or earlier (e.g. WHERE object_end_date <= 1839)  
• `objects.title`: return in the final answer  
• `objects.medium`: return in the final answer  
• `images.object_id`: join‐key to `objects`  
• `images.original_image_url`: return in the final answer  

Typical filter conditions  
• `department = 'Photographs'`  
• `LOWER(object_name) LIKE '%photograph%'`  
• `object_end_date <= 1839`  
• `LOWER(artist_display_name) NOT LIKE 'unknown%'`  

Below are ten exploratory / incremental queries (each returns ≤ 20 rows) that gradually build toward the final answer.  

```sql
-- 1. Preview object names that contain “photograph”
SELECT DISTINCT object_name
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects`
WHERE LOWER(object_name) LIKE '%photograph%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Inspect departments for those objects
SELECT DISTINCT department
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects`
WHERE LOWER(object_name) LIKE '%photograph%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Get basic object info within the Photographs department
SELECT object_id, title, artist_display_name, object_end_date
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects`
WHERE department = 'Photographs'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Add the “Photograph” word filter and check date distribution
SELECT object_id, object_end_date, object_name
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects`
WHERE department = 'Photographs'
  AND LOWER(object_name) LIKE '%photograph%'
ORDER BY object_end_date
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Exclude unknown artists
SELECT object_id, title, artist_display_name
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects`
WHERE department = 'Photographs'
  AND LOWER(object_name) LIKE '%photograph%'
  AND LOWER(artist_display_name) NOT LIKE 'unknown%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Add the 1839 date condition
SELECT object_id, title, artist_display_name, object_end_date
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects`
WHERE department = 'Photographs'
  AND LOWER(object_name) LIKE '%photograph%'
  AND LOWER(artist_display_name) NOT LIKE 'unknown%'
  AND object_end_date <= 1839
ORDER BY object_end_date
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Bring in medium information
SELECT object_id, title, artist_display_name, medium
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects`
WHERE department = 'Photographs'
  AND LOWER(object_name) LIKE '%photograph%'
  AND LOWER(artist_display_name) NOT LIKE 'unknown%'
  AND object_end_date <= 1839
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Look up any image rows tied to those object_ids
SELECT DISTINCT img.object_id, img.original_image_url
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.images` AS img
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects` AS obj
  ON img.object_id = obj.object_id
WHERE obj.department = 'Photographs'
  AND LOWER(obj.object_name) LIKE '%photograph%'
  AND LOWER(obj.artist_display_name) NOT LIKE 'unknown%'
  AND obj.object_end_date <= 1839
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Combine object details with one image URL per object
SELECT DISTINCT
  obj.object_id,
  obj.title,
  obj.artist_display_name,
  obj.medium,
  img.original_image_url
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects`  AS obj
LEFT JOIN `bigquery-public-data.the_met.images` AS img
  ON obj.object_id = img.object_id
WHERE obj.department = 'Photographs'
  AND LOWER(obj.object_name) LIKE '%photograph%'
  AND LOWER(obj.artist_display_name) NOT LIKE 'unknown%'
  AND obj.object_end_date <= 1839
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final answer: titles, artist names, mediums, and original image URLs
SELECT DISTINCT
  obj.title                            AS title,
  obj.artist_display_name              AS artist_name,
  obj.medium                           AS medium,
  img.original_image_url               AS original_image_url
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects`  AS obj
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.the_met.images`   AS img
  ON obj.object_id = img.object_id
WHERE obj.department = 'Photographs'
  AND LOWER(obj.object_name) LIKE '%photograph%'
  AND LOWER(obj.artist_display_name) NOT LIKE 'unknown%'
  AND obj.object_end_date <= 1839
LIMIT 20;
```
